# CLAUDE.md

{{title}} is a NativeDesktop app: a Rust view tree that renders to native widgets (AppKit on
macOS) through the `nd` crate. It starts as a click counter in `src/app.rs`.

## Commands

- `cargo run`: open the app. `{{env}}_DEMO=1` starts it in demo mode (fixed state).
- `nd check`: fmt, clippy with the framework lint table, framework lints and the appearance
  audit (`tests/appearance.rs`). Run before every commit.
- `nd test`: tiers 1 and 2. `nd test --tier real` runs tier 3 (needs a window server).
- `nd check --release` also fails while the README still has its `nd:` HTML-comment placeholders.

## Rules

- Use intents, not `cfg`. Say `scaffold()`, `toolbar()`, `titlebar()`; do not branch on the OS in
  view code. `cfg(target_os)` belongs in native widget modules, with a reason comment elsewhere.
- Colours, radii, spacing and fonts come from tokens (`cx.theme()`), never literals. Colour
  constructors live in the theme file only.
- Every window you add gets a `.window(..)` in `tests/appearance.rs`: the audit fails any
  colour that is not a theme token and any text under WCAG contrast, in light, dark and matugen.
- Any list that can pass 50 rows uses `list()`. No scroll container fed by `.children(..)`.
- Floating things (menus, popovers, tooltips) go through `cx.overlay` or a built-in.
- Timers run on the executor. No `Instant::now`, `thread::sleep` or `smol::Timer` in UI code.
- The OS draws its own structure: sidebar, toolbar, window controls, sheets, menus. Do not build a
  replica. `.drawn()` needs a comment saying why the native control cannot do the job.
- No inline SVG. Use the icon set.
- Name `gpui` and `objc2` only inside native widget modules.
- Keep views small. State lives in entities, views read it in `render`.
- Test in the tier that matches the behaviour: logic in tier 1 (`tests/app.rs`, `nd::test::TestApp`,
  no window), looks in tier 2, OS-owned behaviour in tier 3.

A finding from `nd check` prints as `file:line:col: [rule] message`. To silence one with a reason,
put `// nd-allow(rule): reason` on the line or the line above.

## Debugging

Read `nd diagnose --last` before reproducing a bug.
